{"format":"tvf-scene","v":1,"name":"example · rates, not angles","loop":54,"ease":"inout","hold":0,"gravity":1,"wind":0,"trail":null,"camera":[{"t":0,"box":[-0.4875,-0.0525,-0.165,0.4275]},{"t":0.17,"box":[-0.4875,-0.0525,-0.165,0.4275]},{"t":0.2,"box":[-0.054636017,-0.0546360015,0.600996002,0.227136002]},{"t":0.36,"box":[-0.054636017,-0.0546360015,0.600996002,0.227136002]},{"t":0.4,"box":[-0.4938816,-0.0588816,0.6052416,0.4188816]},{"t":0.52,"box":[-0.4938816,-0.0588816,0.6052416,0.4188816]},{"t":0.55,"box":[-0.48,-0.045,-0.1725,0.42]},{"t":0.86,"box":[-0.48,-0.045,-0.1725,0.42]},{"t":0.9,"box":[-0.4938816,-0.0588816,0.6052416,0.4188816]}],"stops":[0.17,0.36,0.52,0.7,0.86],"beats":[{"title":"Six in twelve","text":"A carpenter calls a roof *six in twelve*: it [rises six](#lit:4) for every [twelve it runs](#lit:2). Nobody on the site needs the angle; the pitch is had with a level and a tape.\n\nThe pitch is a rate, **of** something **per** something: rise per run. Drag the pitch and watch the roof."},{"title":"The hand's two rates","text":"A [point runs over the circle](#lit:14) on a chord. From one end the [ray](#lit:12) turns a quarter; from the middle the [radius](#lit:13) turns a half.\n\nAgainst the straight chord, the sweep comes at [arc over chord](#lit:21,23), climbing to **π/2**, or [chord over arc](#lit:22,24), falling to **2/π**. Never at [the writer's 1](#lit:19)."},{"title":"The corner, where three meet","text":"At the corner the roof is [twelve in twelve](#lit:3,4,7): v fills exactly as fast as h empties, and their ratio is 1.\n\nThe running rates there are 1.1107 and 0.9003, not 1. The writer's 1 sits **between** them: the geometric mean of π/2 and 2/π."},{"title":"The Cauchy is a speed","text":"Turn a ray from the eave in equal steps and mark where it meets the post. Below the corner the [marks crowd](#lit:28,29,30,31,32); past it they [run away](#lit:34,35), the last at the horizon.\n\nHalf the steps lie [below the corner](#lit:33). That is the Cauchy: **turn per reading**, the per against itself, no payload in it."},{"title":"Readers compose, writers count the turn","text":"A pitch of [six in twelve](#lit:36) turned on by four in twelve lands on [twelve in twelve](#lit:37): **½ ⊕ ⅓ = 1**, by tangent addition, (s + t)/(1 − st). Every number stays rational.\n\nThe degrees, 26.57° + 18.43° = 45°, need π: a share of the whole turn, which only the writer holds."},{"title":"Writers have angles; readers have sweeps","text":"The roof's pitch and the protractor's degree name the same direction. The pitch is the reader's; the degree, π/2 and 2/π are the writer's measure of the sweep, and the writer's 1 is had only by joining both.\n\nThe carpenter's is the one the reader has. [The essay, §11](https://github.com/reportbase/wander/blob/main/papers/essays/14-rates-not-angles.md)"}],"path":null,"items":[{"fill":{"color":"#f4f1ea","opacity":1},"stroke":null,"width":0,"open":false,"exact":{"x":[-0.9,0.9,0.9,-0.9],"y":[0.675,0.675,-0.675,-0.675],"r":null,"smooth":null,"ctrl":null,"holes":[]}},{"morph":0},{"morph":1},{"morph":2},{"morph":3},{"morph":4},{"morph":27},{"morph":28},{"morph":29},{"morph":30},{"morph":31},{"morph":32},{"morph":33},{"morph":34},{"morph":35},{"morph":7},{"morph":36},{"morph":37},{"morph":8},{"morph":9},{"morph":10},{"morph":11},{"morph":12},{"morph":13},{"morph":14},{"morph":17},{"morph":18},{"morph":19},{"morph":21},{"morph":22},{"morph":23},{"morph":24},{"morph":5},{"morph":39},{"morph":40},{"morph":41},{"morph":42},{"morph":43},{"morph":6},{"morph":44},{"morph":45},{"morph":46},{"morph":47},{"morph":48},{"morph":49},{"morph":15},{"morph":16},{"morph":50},{"morph":25},{"morph":51},{"morph":52},{"morph":26},{"morph":53},{"morph":54},{"morph":20},{"morph":38},{"morph":55},{"morph":56},{"morph":57},{"morph":58},{"morph":59},{"morph":60},{"morph":61},{"morph":62},{"morph":63},{"morph":64}],"morphs":[{"exact":true,"open":true,"holes":null,"keys":[{"x":[-0.435,-0.2175],"y":[-5.55111512e-17,-5.55111512e-17]